#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087473 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a4168b-1425-5f3a-a577-4b5884906a52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/id #uuid "ad30d35a-4fd5-593e-bb61-a3ac833668a5" :question/math-academy-id "e-5252" :question/problem "If $z=7-3\\textrm{i}$, calculate $z+\\overline{z}$." :question/worked-solution "*Method 1*\n\nWhen we add a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always twice the real part of the complex number.\n\nFor the given complex number\n\n$$\nz=7-3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nthe real part is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{Re}(z) = 7\n$$\n\nso we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz + z^(―) &= 2Re(z) \\\\\n&= 2(7) \\\\\n&= 14\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Method 2*\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of adding the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number\n\n$$\nz=7-3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nwe flip the sign of the imaginary part and get\n\n$$\n\\overline{z} = 7 + 3 \\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nAdding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz + z^(―) &= (7 - 3\\textrm{i}) + (7 + 3\\textrm{i}) \\\\\n&= (7 + 7) + (-3\\textrm{i} + 3\\textrm{i}) \\\\\n&= 14 + \\textrm{i}0 \\\\\n&= 14\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087474 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64cd3ef1-6d41-50c6-b09d-cb709d89281f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Product of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/id #uuid "135dcf7f-99e7-5ad0-b142-b9782fbc5fb3" :question/math-academy-id "e-5254" :question/problem "Given that $z=7-4\\textrm{i}$, calculate $z\\overline{z}$." :question/worked-solution "*Method 1*\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number\n\n$$\nz=7-4\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nthe real part is\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Re}(z)=7\n$$\n\nand the imaginary part is\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Im}(z)=-4\n$$\n\nso we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nzz^(―) &= (Re(z))^{2} + (Im(z))^{2} \\\\\n&= 7^{2} + (-4)^{2} \\\\\n&= 49 + 16 \\\\\n&= 65\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Method 2*\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number\n\n$$\nz=7-4\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nwe flip the sign of the imaginary part and get\n\n$$\n\\overline{z} = 7 + 4 \\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nzz^(―) &= (7 - 4\\textrm{i})(7 + 4\\textrm{i}) \\\\\n&= 7^{2} + (7)(4)\\textrm{i} + (-4)(7)\\textrm{i} - (4)^{2}\\textrm{i}^{2} \\\\\n&= 49 + 28\\textrm{i} - 28\\textrm{i} - (16)(-1) \\\\\n&= 49 + 16 \\\\\n&= 65\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264838 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64cd3ef1-6d41-50c6-b09d-cb709d89281f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Product of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2f8ac60-74d2-52a1-9616-61f99773804b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264840} {:answer/id #uuid "1db4ff04-3eaa-5d46-979b-e92e8a439648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264841} {:answer/id #uuid "aee1a11d-6dbe-57f7-b668-d0cc72ca05ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264842} {:answer/id #uuid "8d209136-f6b9-5f52-80cd-705074430166" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264843} {:answer/id #uuid "7ad7c719-0e5a-5d78-a6ad-8e1254509584" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ad7c719-0e5a-5d78-a6ad-8e1254509584" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264844} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6a95aee-abb9-5cff-980f-0010527f0794" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264839}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cb021f36-74b8-5fbc-ac1d-0f42467d1ae6" :question/math-academy-id "q-159758" :question/problem "Given that $z=9+3\\text{i},$ calculate $z\\overset{―}{z}.$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=9+3\\text{i},$ the real part is $\\text{Re}(z)=9,$ and the imaginary part is $\\text{Im}(z)=3,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(\\text{Re}(z))^{2}+(\\text{Im}(z))^{2} \\\\  & ={9}^{2}+{3}^{2} \\\\  & =81+9 \\\\  & =90.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=9+3\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=9-3\\text{i}.$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(9+3\\text{i})(9-3\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={9}^{2}+(9)(3)\\text{i}+(-3)(9)\\text{i}-{\\text{i}}^{2}(3)^{2} \\\\  & =81+27\\text{i}-27\\text{i}-(-1)(9) \\\\  & =81+9 \\\\  & =90.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264845 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a4168b-1425-5f3a-a577-4b5884906a52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2efb9f42-795f-599c-bf9b-26642e0be7f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10+10\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264847} {:answer/id #uuid "dfadec77-63ca-5147-b925-771712dfe5b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264848} {:answer/id #uuid "98dd36f1-8c49-51f3-bd2a-dfaf9d9e8fce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264849} {:answer/id #uuid "75f62974-051c-52c3-b266-9f399073c7d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264850} {:answer/id #uuid "7d90a08a-dd15-5e7d-940e-b2b7844eb330" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfadec77-63ca-5147-b925-771712dfe5b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264848} :answer-field/id #uuid "55d6996e-ec7f-54bb-96fb-cd07236f661c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264846}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31e8a2e3-0eb3-54aa-baf3-11e84b9b6b43" :question/math-academy-id "q-16419" :question/problem "If $z=5+5\\text{i}$, calculate $z+\\overset{―}{z}.$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we add a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always twice the real part of the complex number.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=5+5\\text{i},$ the real part is $Re(z)=5,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =2\\text{Re}(z) \\\\  & =2(5) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of adding the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=5+5\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=5-5\\text{i}.$\n\nAdding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =(5+5\\text{i})+(5-5\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(5+5)+\\text{i}(5-5) \\\\  & =10+\\text{i}0 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264852 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a4168b-1425-5f3a-a577-4b5884906a52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6adbc1e3-3d82-5178-8b83-a1f288ac56d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6adbc1e3-3d82-5178-8b83-a1f288ac56d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264854} :answer-field/id #uuid "87422d32-116a-57b0-ac9a-4205ed614475" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264853}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1de0640a-2c8c-5939-afc7-2ab4ac7aafb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-279463" :question/problem "If $z=6-10\\text{i}$, then $z+\\overset{―}{z}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we add a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always twice the real part of the complex number.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=6-10\\text{i},$ the real part is $Re(z)=6,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =2\\text{Re}(z) \\\\  & =2(6) \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of adding the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=6-10\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=6+10\\text{i}.$\n\nAdding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =(6-10\\text{i})+(6+10\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(6+6)+\\text{i}(-10+10) \\\\  & =12+\\text{i}0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64cd3ef1-6d41-50c6-b09d-cb709d89281f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Product of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9d8fe9a-f154-53b7-9965-c0a1e8dd7f4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9d8fe9a-f154-53b7-9965-c0a1e8dd7f4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264857} :answer-field/id #uuid "67468291-493e-580f-b521-868c42ee270b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264856}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae6e4698-a407-5efb-9c25-7234c8cc2dd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-279470" :question/problem "If $z=-6+\\text{i},$ then $z\\overset{―}{z}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=-6+\\text{i},$ the real part is $\\text{Re}(z)=6,$ and the imaginary part is $\\text{Im}(z)=1,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(\\text{Re}(z))^{2}+(\\text{Im}(z))^{2} \\\\  & =(-6)^{2}+{1}^{2} \\\\  & =36+1 \\\\  & =37.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=-6+\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=-6-\\text{i}.$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(-6+\\text{i})(-6-\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(-6)^{2}+(-6)(-1)\\text{i}+(1)(-6)\\text{i}-{\\text{i}}^{2}(1)^{2} \\\\  & =36+\\cancel{6\\text{i}}-\\cancel{6\\text{i}}-(-1)(1) \\\\  & =36+1 \\\\  & =37.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264858 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64cd3ef1-6d41-50c6-b09d-cb709d89281f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Product of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a912c6e-2a55-50bb-9ac7-afba784111a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a912c6e-2a55-50bb-9ac7-afba784111a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264860} :answer-field/id #uuid "461ff513-85b1-5bf5-9c70-d8ec1fb6ac3e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264859}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d8f85871-8277-5c6c-a96a-216de2cb3642" :question/math-academy-id "q-279472" :question/problem "If $z=-2+7\\text{i},$ then $z\\overset{―}{z}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=-2+7\\text{i},$ the real part is $\\text{Re}(z)=-2,$ and the imaginary part is $\\text{Im}(z)=7,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(\\text{Re}(z))^{2}+(\\text{Im}(z))^{2} \\\\  & =(-2)^{2}+{7}^{2} \\\\  & =4+49 \\\\  & =53.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=-2+7\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=-2-7\\text{i}.$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(-2+7\\text{i})(-2-7\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(-2)^{2}+(-2)(-7)\\text{i}+(7)(-2)\\text{i}-{\\text{i}}^{2}(7)^{2} \\\\  & =4+\\cancel{14\\text{i}}-\\cancel{14\\text{i}}-(-1)(49) \\\\  & =4+49 \\\\  & =53.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264861 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64cd3ef1-6d41-50c6-b09d-cb709d89281f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Product of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e6d14ad-400d-59e3-9fee-6140065b9e7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264863} {:answer/id #uuid "bd6104a2-fe8b-5e05-ad9a-6306d5728a87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "73" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd6104a2-fe8b-5e05-ad9a-6306d5728a87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "73" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264864} :answer-field/id #uuid "fba4a822-de09-55ca-ab9b-4a8a9cbf1ed0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264862}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3e03097f-25e9-5676-8547-e2a4836c4d10" :question/math-academy-id "q-279479" :question/problem "If $z=-3-8\\text{i}$, then $z\\overset{―}{z}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=-3-8\\text{i},$ the real part is $\\text{Re}(z)=-3,$ and the imaginary part is $\\text{Im}(z)=-8,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(\\text{Re}(z))^{2}+(\\text{Im}(z))^{2} \\\\  & =(-3)^{2}+(-8)^{2} \\\\  & =9+64 \\\\  & =73.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=-3-8\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=-3+8\\text{i}.$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(-3-8\\text{i})(-3+8\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(3)^{2}+(-3)(8)\\text{i}+(-8)(-3)\\text{i}-{\\text{i}}^{2}(8)^{2} \\\\  & =9-\\cancel{24\\text{i}}+\\cancel{24\\text{i}}-(-1)(64) \\\\  & =9+64 \\\\  & =73.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a4168b-1425-5f3a-a577-4b5884906a52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75384022-9548-5c49-af07-35925da30071" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264867} {:answer/id #uuid "df678345-7c69-5b20-a7ac-4b8b4b98d2b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264868} {:answer/id #uuid "f4f90229-e4a1-56d0-95d2-21d1d2037a28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264869} {:answer/id #uuid "4ac4bdfa-897d-5fe2-8fba-1cfead55f231" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264870} {:answer/id #uuid "de5f9968-21f3-5cdb-b66f-a88348214cf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-10\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ac4bdfa-897d-5fe2-8fba-1cfead55f231" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264870} :answer-field/id #uuid "e277e1b7-f330-56d2-afe0-12b8aa73127d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264866}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f657637c-aa1a-591d-a34f-42c85fc03be9" :question/math-academy-id "q-71984" :question/problem "If $z=3+5\\text{i}$, calculate $z+\\overset{―}{z}.$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we add a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always twice the real part of the complex number.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=3+5\\text{i},$ the real part is $Re(z)=3,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =2\\text{Re}(z) \\\\  & =2(3) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of adding the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=3+5\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=3-5\\text{i}.$\n\nAdding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =(3+5\\text{i})+(3-5\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(3+3)+\\text{i}(5-5) \\\\  & =6+\\text{i}0 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264872 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a4168b-1425-5f3a-a577-4b5884906a52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "402c6b2d-0ac1-5c1a-b38a-5ba938f1ce74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264874} {:answer/id #uuid "fa580ef5-7b15-581d-93d6-0d9fbfb79fba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264875} {:answer/id #uuid "eefc7ef9-5e52-5cbb-ba38-16df4cea56d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264876} {:answer/id #uuid "7594410a-7f01-5c04-a747-38ae6d639cf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264877} {:answer/id #uuid "5f85ad16-c69c-5343-9af4-cd1f4f125422" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8+14\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa580ef5-7b15-581d-93d6-0d9fbfb79fba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264875} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5fd970f-898a-5707-aad9-e3983188c49f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264873}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5aa2c32e-1630-5557-b712-bf9edc8bbed7" :question/math-academy-id "q-71986" :question/problem "If $z=4+7\\text{i}$, calculate $z+\\overset{―}{z}.$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we add a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always twice the real part of the complex number.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=4+7\\text{i},$ the real part is $Re(z)=4,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =2\\text{Re}(z) \\\\  & =2(4) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of adding the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=4+7\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=4-7\\text{i}.$\n\nAdding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =(4+7\\text{i})+(4-7\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(4+4)+\\text{i}(7-7) \\\\  & =8+\\text{i}0 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264879 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a4168b-1425-5f3a-a577-4b5884906a52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26197e56-c03f-588d-9089-73a6516ca2a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264881} {:answer/id #uuid "d88468a9-7ac6-5911-99ee-44a3998a18b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264882} {:answer/id #uuid "dd4c648e-8deb-5db4-accb-8562e0d53db5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264883} {:answer/id #uuid "2f1c59eb-377e-50c4-be6a-71f54b7a904f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16+4\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264884} {:answer/id #uuid "1a558f5c-7100-594d-938c-bafee016dd38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d88468a9-7ac6-5911-99ee-44a3998a18b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264882} :answer-field/id #uuid "8011169d-1837-5a72-be1f-8040492ae243" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264880}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6a6db4d5-e37b-564c-bcd8-fef40005ff98" :question/math-academy-id "q-71987" :question/problem "If $z=-8+2\\text{i}$, calculate $z+\\overset{―}{z}.$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we add a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always twice the real part of the complex number.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=-8+2\\text{i},$ the real part is $Re(z)=-8,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =2\\text{Re}(z) \\\\  & =2(-8) \\\\  & =-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of adding the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=-8+2\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=-8-2\\text{i}.$\n\nAdding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =(-8+2\\text{i})+(-8-2\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(-8+(-8))+\\text{i}(2-2) \\\\  & =-16+\\text{i}0 \\\\  & =-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64cd3ef1-6d41-50c6-b09d-cb709d89281f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Product of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74983a08-0f6c-5edb-92fe-bc13d11a4586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264888} {:answer/id #uuid "b1668985-4a8b-5600-838a-54196ea0cad0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264889} {:answer/id #uuid "25ddc0b7-b5e1-5d43-ab34-e7f7df5d70cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264890} {:answer/id #uuid "abe138b2-1301-5695-86e1-7793505ccb80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264891} {:answer/id #uuid "d723c870-2bd4-53a2-bbe4-48f8fe421b38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d723c870-2bd4-53a2-bbe4-48f8fe421b38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264892} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c470d82-0a80-56f9-85de-823e5e993ad7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264887}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4269613b-9e4c-59b0-b903-a46d5d3219ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-71989" :question/problem "Given that $z=8+6\\text{i}$, calculate $z\\overset{―}{z}.$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=8+6\\text{i},$ the real part is $\\text{Re}(z)=8,$ and the imaginary part is $\\text{Im}(z)=6,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(\\text{Re}(z))^{2}+(\\text{Im}(z))^{2} \\\\  & ={8}^{2}+{6}^{2} \\\\  & =64+36 \\\\  & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=8+6\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=8-6\\text{i}.$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(8+6\\text{i})(8-6\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={8}^{2}+(8)(6)\\text{i}+(-6)(8)\\text{i}-{\\text{i}}^{2}(6)^{2} \\\\  & =64+48\\text{i}-48\\text{i}-(-1)(36) \\\\  & =64+36 \\\\  & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
